  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. The premise that `channel` is no longer read doesn't hold, at least according to the contracts in this repo.\n\n**`contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json`** shows the `analytics-ingest` consumer at `deployedVersion: 3`, and it lists `channel` as a required field on `OrderPlaced`:\n\n```json\n\"channel\": \"enum:web|store|marketplace\",\n```\n\nIf I take `channel` out of the event (`src/core/events.ts:16,50`), `npm run contracts` (`scripts/verify-contracts.mjs`, the ARCH-4 event-contract check) will fail. More importantly, analytics-ingest's production deployment would start getting events without a field it requires.\n\nTaking it out of the order model goes further. `src/core/order.ts` validates `channel` as part of `POST /orders` input, and `src/api/requestParsing.ts` parses it. The documented `createApp` request shape in CLAUDE.md and README.md includes it too. Without `channel` on the order, the event has nowhere to get it from, so both changes go together.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n\n1. **Hold off** until analytics-ingest stops requiring `channel`. That would mean they ship a new contract version without it and update their contract file here. Then I can remove it cleanly.\n2. **Go ahead anyway** if you know analytics-ingest has already stopped using it and the contract file here is out of date. In that case I'd remove the field everywhere (event, model, validation, request parsing, tests, contract-check sample, docs) and update or remove the `channel` entry in that contract file. That contract change is really analytics-ingest's decision, so it should be confirmed with them.\n3. **Remove it from the order model only** if you don't want to touch the event. That doesn't work on its own, because the event needs the value from somewhere.\n\nWho told you it's no longer read? If it was the analytics team, option 2 may be fine once their contract is updated.",
